   "id": "bekhorot.29b.10",
   "daf": "29b",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "אֲבָל לוֹקְחִין מִמֶּנּוּ טְוִי וּבְגָדִים. הַשְׁתָּא טְוִי זָבְנִינַן, בְּגָדִים מִיבַּעְיָא? מַאי בְּגָדִים? נַמְטֵי.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «But one» may «purchase spun» thread «from him, and» all the more so one may purchase «garments» from him. The Gemara asks: «Now» that the mishna has taught that «we may purchase spun» thread from one who is suspect with regard to firstborn, «is» it «necessary» to teach that one may purchase «garments?» The Gemara answers: «What» does the mishna mean which it says: «Garments?» It is referring to «felt [namtei]» garments, which are not made of spun thread."
  }
 ],
